<title>SOUTH KOREA: Midopa places convertible bonds.</title>
<headline>Midopa places convertible bonds.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Midopa Department Store privately placed 10 billion won worth of convertible bonds to raise funds for operations, a company statement said on Friday.</p>
<p>Daishin Factoring Co Ltd underwrote the bonds, which were issued on Thursday, it said.</p>
<p>The bonds carry a coupon of five percent per annum and will mature on June 26, 2000.</p>
<p>The bonds can be converted into Midopa's common shares between June 27, 1998 and May 31, 2000 at 8,028 won per share, the statement said.</p>
<p>Midopa shares were down 50 won at 7,700 in early Friday morning trading.</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom 9822) 727 5643</p>
</text>
